course: dictionary
lesson: 4830
title: One word, many meanings: hush
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and hush is a good example. It can be a verb, a noun, or a single word shouted as a command. The words around it tell you which meaning you need.
explain: «Hush, little baby» means a parent is making a baby quiet and calm. «A hush fell over the room» is different: a hush is a sudden quiet, when everyone stops talking at once. The spelling stays the same, but the job the word does changes.
explain: Hush can also mean keeping something secret. «They tried to hush it up» means hiding something bad so people do not find out. Hush-hush means secret, and hush money is money paid to keep someone quiet. Ask yourself: is someone being told to be quiet, or is something being kept secret?
fact: Hush can be a verb, a noun or a command, so check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: «Hush!» as a command means «Be quiet!»
fact: A hush is a sudden quiet, when everyone stops talking.
fact: «Hush up» means keeping something secret, often something bad.
fact: Hush-hush is an informal word meaning secret.
exercise: The Rabbit whispers, «Oh, hush!» to Alice. What does hush mean here? | Tell everybody the news | Go to sleep forever | *Be quiet! | Sing a song softly
exercise: «A hush fell over the room just before the magician appeared.» What is a hush here? | A type of magic trick | A soft pillow | A loud noise from the audience | *A sudden quiet, when everyone stops talking
exercise: The newspaper says the council tried to hush it up. What does hush it up mean? | Make a loud announcement | Tell everyone straight away | *Keep it secret so people do not find out | Shout about it on the radio
test: Mum sings a lullaby and says, «Hush, little baby.» What does hush mean here? | Give the baby a bath | Count the baby's toes | Wake the baby up | *Make the baby calm and quiet
test: Ella says, «It's hush-hush, so don't tell anyone.» What does hush-hush mean? | Happy and bright | *Secret | Cold and wet | Loud and busy
exam: Which sentence uses hush as a noun? | "Hush!" shouted the teacher | *After the joke, a hush fell over the hall | They tried to hush up the story | Hush the baby gently
